                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "It was a skill issue with me. Got hard stuck on the third boss and bashed my head against a wall for an hour before getting fed up. I had big stamina management issues. I also found it a little difficult to see my own character at times due to the incredibly simple color palate. More than a few times I lost track of which gray shape was me and which was the enemy. \n\nI guess I'm not much one for 2D combat. I also bounced off of Hollow Knight pretty hard (even though I did begrudgingly finish that one). I could already feel myself rushing through this game fairly early on; not exploring every path. The combat just didn't do it for me, so I began skipping enemy encounters when I could by running past them. \n\nIf you're someone who likes this general genre of souls-like metroidvania, you'll probably enjoy Unworthy as well. I'll stick with 3D souls-likes from now on though. I've learned that the 2D flavor just isn't for me.",
